<BaseLayout title="Editorial standards and change log" description="How AI Amigos authors, sources, tests, reviews, corrects, and discloses practical AI records."><div class="shell reading"><p class="eyebrow">Trust and editorial method</p><h1>Useful AI guidance should show its work.</h1><p class="lede">AI Amigos separates authorship, historical provenance, current testing, editorial review, independent review, and production proof so a visitor can see exactly what has and has not been verified.</p>
<h2>People and review ownership</h2><p><a href="/about/vijay-bhoyar/"><strong>Vijay Bhoyar</strong></a> directs the project and is the named author of the current working evidence specifications. The <strong>AI Amigos Editorial Desk</strong> remains an organizational byline for source-preserved legacy material and internal protocol checks. Neither role is described as independent domain review. Outside review requires a named reviewer, qualification, exact version, scope, conflict disclosure, and independently controlled verification.</p>
<h2>Publication gate</h2><ol><li>Define one distinct job to be done and intended audience.</li><li>Use at least two authoritative external sources; prefer primary evidence.</li><li>Provide actionable steps, a worked example, limitations, and a practical artifact.</li><li>Name the author, reviewer, review date, next review date, and substantive changes.</li><li>Require explicit human approval before editorial publication.</li></ol>
<h2>Evidence tiers</h2><dl><dt><strong>Independent</strong></dt><dd>Issued and controlled by an outside organization, publisher, reviewer, or adopter.</dd><dt><strong>Jointly verified</strong></dt><dd>Prepared with AI Amigos and explicitly verified by an outside participant.</dd><dt><strong>Author controlled</strong></dt><dd>Published by AI Amigos; useful for provenance but not independent recognition.</dd></dl>
<h2>Outcome and benchmark gate</h2><ol><li>A private project records the baseline, experiment versions, test cases, human decisions, and follow-up outcome.</li><li>Only deliberately sanitized fields can enter a proof-pack submission.</li><li>A reviewer checks privacy, claim scope, evidence lineage, and limitations.</li><li>Approved public records retain versions and correction history.</li><li>Benchmark cohorts remain suppressed below 10 reviewed reports, below three independent organizations, or when one organization supplies more than half the cohort.</li></ol>
<h2>Review intervals</h2><ul><li>90 days: vendors, products, careers, technical guides, and working methods.</li><li>180 days: evergreen foundations.</li><li>Gated review: healthcare, finance, safety, credentials, legal, or other high-stakes claims.</li></ul>
<h2>Status language</h2><dl><dt><strong>Source preserved</strong></dt><dd>The historical route and date remain, but the page has not passed the evidence gate. It is noindex and excluded from discovery.</dd><dt><strong>Editorial protocol</strong></dt><dd>Internal structure, privacy boundary, sources, limitations, and dates passed editorial review. It is not an outcome claim.</dd><dt><strong>Reviewed outcome</strong></dt><dd>A sanitized run report and follow-up measurement passed the stated review gate.</dd><dt><strong>Benchmark</strong></dt><dd>A multi-organization cohort passed sample, comparability, privacy, concentration, methodology, and review gates.</dd></dl>
<h2>Corrections and disclosure</h2><p>Send corrections, source suggestions, review proposals, or adoption verification through <a href="/contact/">contact actions</a>. Material corrections remain in the <a href="/corrections/">correction registry</a>. AI may help prepare drafts and checks; a person must approve publication. Funding, affiliate, vendor, reviewer, or participant relationships must be disclosed on the affected record.</p>
<h2>Public change log</h2><ul><li><strong>2026-08-25 · v0.1.1:</strong> Released three schema-validated synthetic method examples, four governed pilot packages, downloadable participant and proof-pack records, an external reviewer kit, and a SHA-256 release manifest. These are method and readiness artifacts, not adoption or outcome evidence.</li><li><strong>2026-08-25:</strong> Published the defined endeavor, three author-controlled working methods, evidence tiers, public claim ledger, empty independent-evidence registries, named project authorship, multi-organization benchmark gates, evidence schemas, and private counsel-data boundary.</li><li><strong>2026-08-24:</strong> Released the verified practice network, local project dashboard, four editorial reference protocols, benchmark suppression, field challenges, and legacy-guide quarantine.</li><li><strong>2026-08-23:</strong> Added the local-first workbench, seven-stage proof loop, proof-pack boundary, and optional account architecture.</li><li><strong>2026-08-22:</strong> Added four tracks, five local-only tools, twenty templates, and inactive-by-default external integrations.</li></ul><p><a href="/timeline/">Open the full public timeline →</a></p></div></BaseLayout>
